{
  "$schema": "https://go.kicad.org/pcm/schemas/v1",
  "name": "Via Stitching",
  "description": "Stitch copper zones together with a grid of vias on a chosen net",
  "description_full": "Fills the overlap of a net's copper zones (for example the top and bottom GND pours) with a grid of stitching vias, on whichever two copper layers you pick.\n\nBuilt on KiCad's modern IPC API, so it keeps working on KiCad 11 and later, where the legacy SWIG pcbnew bindings are removed.\n\nFeatures:\n- Through, Micro, Blind, Buried, and Blind/Buried via types, on any layer pair.\n- Hexagonal, square, or staggered patterns, with configurable diameter, drill, and spacing.\n- X/Y offset for stitching more than one pattern onto the same area without overlap.\n- Automatically avoids other nets' tracks, pads, zones, and existing holes, with proper clearances.\n- Select an existing via to clone its settings, or let the dialog remember your last run.\n- Placed vias are grouped together so they can be deleted as a set.\n- Dialog follows KiCad's own configured UI language: English, Dutch, German, or French.",
